# Pairs with RoutingConverges. An undo before the flip clears T's forwarding
# but not a fence the interrupted swap left, so T stays in Rejecting under an
# alias that still names it and its own pair is refused forever. Fairness is
# unchanged.
MODULE: RoutingConvergesUndoBeforeFlipKeepsFence
TARGET: RoutingConverges
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: an undo before the flip leaves a fence in place, so the tree's own copy refuses forever
PERTURBS: UndoBeforeFlip

--- FIND
    /\ rz \in {"snap", "copied"}
    /\ fence' = {}
    /\ rz' = "undone"
--- REPLACE
    /\ rz \in {"snap", "copied"}
\* MUTATION: the fence is not lifted.
    /\ fence' = fence
    /\ rz' = "undone"
--- END